WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.530
Welcome to Quantitative management and high maturity. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Recognize what makes quantitative process management more than reporting..

2
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:24.020
Consider this scenario. An organization shows dozens of charts but cannot explain sources, variation or decisions. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:35.160
Start with two steps: Set quality and performance objectives. Then Build reliable operational definitions. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:45.800
Continue with Analyze stability and variation. Then Select and evaluate process improvements. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:57.060
Stronger evidence looks like this: Evidence of actual implementation. Weaker evidence would be: An unverified claim. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:11.310
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
